WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.423
"You want to ask Jev to help us spy on Morb?"

2
00:00:16.424 --> 00:00:21.715
Zann stared at Gliss, hardly believing his ears. "Are you kidding?"

3
00:00:21.716 --> 00:00:29.394
"Maybe Gliss is right," Perda said. "I know Jev's not your favorite person, Zann. But he's good at magic."

4
00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:33.744
"So what?" Zann said. "Lots of people are good at magic.

5
00:00:33.745 --> 00:00:36.714
We could ask your parents to help instead.

6
00:00:36.715 --> 00:00:40.499
Or maybe one of our teachers or the mayor."

7
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.027
"It would take too long to explain everything to them," Gliss pointed out.

8
00:00:45.028 --> 00:00:49.153
"Besides, Jev will definitely do it if I ask him."

9
00:00:49.154 --> 00:00:53.890
Zann couldn't believe the girls were seriously thinking about going to Jev for help.

10
00:00:53.891 --> 00:00:57.734
He glanced at Darb, expecting his friend to be on his side.

11
00:00:57.735 --> 00:01:03.363
Darb had a thoughtful look. "Well, it's not a bad idea," he said.

12
00:01:03.364 --> 00:01:05.763
"Let's go find him," Perda said.

13
00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:11.676
Before Zann could say another word, the others were hurrying out of the Hollow.

14
00:01:11.677 --> 00:01:13.855
He had little choice but to follow.

15
00:01:13.856 --> 00:01:17.866
Soon they were all hiding in a clump of trees near Jev's house.

16
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:22.649
Jev was in the yard playing with his pet dragon, but they didn't dare call to him.

17
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:28.275
By now it was afternoon, and there were a lot more people around than there had been earlier.

18
00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:32.217
They all knew that Morb could be awake and lurking out there somewhere.

19
00:01:32.218 --> 00:01:39.217
"I wish we could just use a Summoning spell," Perda complained. "Living without magic is hard!"

20
00:01:39.218 --> 00:01:44.635
"I have an idea." Darb reached into his pocket for a pencil and paper.

21
00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:50.199
Scribbling a note, he held it out to Zing. "Take this to Jev, okay, buddy?"

22
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.725
At first Zing didn't understand what Darb wanted.

23
00:01:53.726 --> 00:02:01.132
He tried to eat the note, and then he tried to roast it. But finally he figured it out.

24
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:05.775
Jev looked up when the dragon flew at him. "Shoo! You'll scare Hazi."

25
00:02:05.776 --> 00:02:09.187
Then he blinked. "Wait a minute. Aren't you . . ."

26
00:02:09.188 --> 00:02:12.269
Zing whistled and dropped the note by Jev's feet.

27
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.525
Jev grabbed the paper and read it.

28
00:02:14.526 --> 00:02:18.525
A second later he picked up his dragon and headed toward his house.

29
00:02:18.526 --> 00:02:24.422
"See?" Zann whispered. "He's ignoring the note! I told you he was—"

30
00:02:24.423 --> 00:02:29.290
"Wait," Gliss interrupted. "He's just putting his dragon inside."

31
00:02:29.291 --> 00:02:32.348
Sure enough, Jev was already hurrying toward them.

32
00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:35.578
When he heard what they wanted, he smirked at Zann.

33
00:02:35.579 --> 00:02:41.835
"Wow, it must be tough living with no magic like a Void all day, huh?" he said.

34
00:02:41.836 --> 00:02:45.124
"Especially for a snooty Red like you."

35
00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:50.138
"Will you help us, Jev?" Gliss asked, grabbing his arm. "Please?"

36
00:02:50.139 --> 00:02:55.669
Jev glanced down at her hand on his arm. "Um, sure," he said.

37
00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.352
"I was just kidding around. What do you want me to do?"

38
00:02:59.353 --> 00:03:03.504
It didn't take long for Jev to summon and send a spy fly to Morb.

39
00:03:03.505 --> 00:03:10.842
Zann watched the whole process, chafing silently at seeing his enemy do magic when he himself was powerless.

40
00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:16.498
"Thanks, Jev," Perda said. "Can you come find us in the Hollow when the spy fly returns?"

41
00:03:16.499 --> 00:03:20.952
"The Hollow?" Jev looked a little nervous. "Sure, I guess."

42
00:03:20.953 --> 00:03:24.333
Just then he noticed Gliss rubbing her stomach.

43
00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:27.519
"Are you hungry? I could conjure up some lunch."

44
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:33.246
"That would be great!" Gliss said. "We haven't eaten since yesterday."

45
00:03:33.247 --> 00:03:38.694
She talked him into conjuring up enough food for all of them, along with some fresh clothes.

46
00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:41.857
After that they left Jev and headed for the Hollow.

47
00:03:41.858 --> 00:03:44.357
When they got there, Zing whimpered.

48
00:03:44.358 --> 00:03:49.916
"I know, Zing," said Zann with a sigh. "I don't like being here either.

49
00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:52.971
But it's safer than being out in the open."

50
00:03:52.972 --> 00:03:57.722
"How long do you think it will take the spy fly to get there and back?" Gliss asked.

51
00:03:57.723 --> 00:04:06.183
The others shrugged. Spy flies were very fast. Like message moths they could zap themselves long distances when necessary.

52
00:04:06.184 --> 00:04:12.216
But there was no way of telling how long it would take the little creature to find Morb and observe what he was doing.

53
00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:16.199
By now Morb had probably woken up and left Zann's house.

54
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:21.480
Zann pulled out Boz's diary. "Guess I'll start reading this while we're waiting.

55
00:04:21.481 --> 00:04:26.059
Maybe we can figure out whether it's still worth trying to get it to the palace."

56
00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:30.862
"Too bad none of us can do an advanced Restore spell yet," Perda said.

57
00:04:30.863 --> 00:04:34.285
"Maybe we could take the diary to Professor Liblow."

58
00:04:34.286 --> 00:04:38.644
"It was dangerous enough to leave the Hollow to find Jev," Darb said.

59
00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:41.870
"Morb and his trolls could be anywhere."

60
00:04:41.871 --> 00:04:48.431
"He's right," Zann agreed. "Besides, we don't even know if we need a Restore spell yet."

61
00:04:48.432 --> 00:04:51.372
Zann opened the diary to the first page.

62
00:04:51.373 --> 00:04:56.245
For a moment he just stared at his grandfather's familiar, loopy handwriting.

63
00:04:56.246 --> 00:05:06.460
Zann had always found it strange that Boz, a highly accomplished Magic Master, chose to record his life in such an old-fashioned and non-magical way.

64
00:05:06.461 --> 00:05:09.804
Pushing that thought aside, Zann started to read.

65
00:05:09.805 --> 00:05:12.643
The diary began before Zann was born.

66
00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:20.218
In fact, one of the earliest entries mentioned Zann's mother—Boz's daughter—meeting a handsome young explorer.

67
00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:23.920
"Dad," Zann murmured, tracing his father's name.

68
00:05:23.921 --> 00:05:27.803
It was tempting to read everything about his parents' early days together.

69
00:05:27.804 --> 00:05:30.319
He knew he didn't have time though.

70
00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.072
He skimmed over some entries about Boz's day-to-day life as a Magic Master.

71
00:05:35.073 --> 00:05:42.960
They were surprisingly boring, but then Zann saw pages filled with stories about his parents' explorations and adventures.

72
00:05:42.961 --> 00:05:48.219
"I can go back and read those later, when Boz is safe," he told himself.

73
00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:54.695
He tore his gaze away from a description of his own third birthday party and continued flipping through the diary.

74
00:05:54.696 --> 00:05:56.830
The next few pages were missing.

75
00:05:56.831 --> 00:06:12.097
When Zann turned to the next legible page, a familiar name jumped out at him; in bold, angry letters, his grandfather had scrawled "Morb."
